.TH "netom\-cli" "1" "FastNetMon Inc"
.SH NAME
netom\-cli \- operational CLI for the netom BGP/BMP engine

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B netom\-cli
[options] [command ...]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspects a running
.BR netom (1)
daemon using router-style commands over its HTTP API. Commands may be given
on the command line, repeated with
.BR \-e ,
piped in on standard input one per line, or typed at an interactive
.B netom>
prompt when
.B netom\-cli
is run with no command and a terminal on standard input.

Keywords may be abbreviated to any unambiguous prefix, so
.B sh ip b sum
is
.BR "show ip bgp summary" .
A
.B ?
at the end of a line lists the keywords that may follow it, always as a
list even when only one keyword matches, and ends the listing with
.B <cr>
when the line is already a command that can be run. In interactive mode TAB
completes instead, and
.B ?
may be pressed at any point in the line without disturbing what has been
typed. The
.B help
command lists every command at once.

This tool is read-only. It issues only GET requests and cannot change the
daemon's state or configuration.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-u\  URL \fR,\ \fB\-\-url= URL
API endpoint, for example
.BR http://127.0.0.1:8080 .
Accepts a bare host or host:port; the port defaults to 8080.

.TP
.BI \-c\  path \fR,\ \fB\-\-config= path
Read the endpoint from a netom configuration file's
.B http_listen
setting.

.TP
.BI \-e\  command \fR,\ \fB\-\-execute= command
Run a command. May be given more than once; commands run in order.

.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit the raw API response instead of a rendered table. Whole-table route
dumps are newline-delimited JSON (one object per line), not a JSON array.

.TP
.BI \-\-timeout\  seconds
Read timeout. Defaults to 120 seconds, which allows for the pauses between
chunks of a large table dump on a busy daemon.

.TP
.B \-h\fR,\ \fB\-\-help
Prints help information

.TP
.B \-V\fR,\ \fB\-\-version
Prints version information

.SH ENDPOINT DISCOVERY
The endpoint is chosen from the first of these that is set:
.BR \-\-url ,
the
.B NETOM_URL
environment variable,
.BR \-c ,
.BR ./netom.conf ,
.BR /etc/netom/netom.conf ,
and finally
.BR http://127.0.0.1:8080 .

A configuration file named explicitly with
.B \-c
that cannot be read, or that sets no usable
.BR http_listen ,
is an error rather than a silent fallback.

netom's shipped default is
.BR "http_listen = [\(dq[::]:8080\(dq]" ,
which is a wildcard and not connectable. Wildcards are rewritten to
loopback:
.B 0.0.0.0
becomes
.BR 127.0.0.1 ,
and
.B ::
becomes
.B ::1
with
.B 127.0.0.1
tried after it. This keeps discovery from ever directing queries off-box on
its own initiative.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B help
Every command in the tree, one per line, with what it shows.
.TP
.B show version
Daemon and CLI versions, uptime and start time.
.TP
.B show status
Configured units and targets, ingress counts, RIB sizes and memory use.
.TP
.B show running\-config
The running configuration, with secrets redacted.
.TP
.B show filters
The Roto script path and source, and the entrypoints netom calls.
.TP
.B show ip bgp summary [bgp|bmp]
One row per neighbor. Add
.B bgp
or
.B bmp
to show only sessions netom terminates itself, or only those observed
through BMP.
.TP
.B show ip bgp neighbors [\fIaddress\fB]
Detailed neighbor information.
.TP
.B show ip bgp [\fIprefix\fB]
Routes for one prefix, or the whole table when no prefix is given.
.TP
.B show ip bgp flowspec [\fIprefix\fB]
FlowSpec rules.
.TP
.B show ipv6 bgp ...
As above, for IPv6.
.TP
.B show bmp routers
Monitored routers feeding BMP to this daemon.
.TP
.B show bmp router \fIid\fB
One monitored router and its BGP sessions.
.TP
.B show ingresses
The raw ingress and session registry.

.SH OUTPUT FILTERS
A command may be followed by
.BR "| include " \fItext\fR,
.BR "| exclude " \fItext\fR,
.BR "| begin " \fItext\fR
or
.BR "| count" .
Matching is case-insensitive substring, not a regular expression.

.SH REPORTED COUNTERS
The counters netom can report are narrower than a router's, and are named
for what they actually are rather than for their Cisco equivalents.

.B UpdRcvd
and
.B NotifRcvd
count UPDATE and NOTIFICATION messages received. There is no sent-message
or total-message counter: netom is a collector and never originates
UPDATEs, and KEEPALIVEs are handled inside the BGP state machine without
being visible to netom. A
.BR MsgRcvd / MsgSent
pair would therefore be fiction.

.B State/PfxRcd
shows the prefix count for an established session netom terminates itself.
For a session observed through BMP it shows
.BR \- ,
because that count would require scanning the whole RIB once per peer.

The count is the number of prefixes the peer currently has in the RIB, not
a running total of announcements, so re-advertisements do not inflate it.
A peer re-announcing a prefix it already announced is performing BGP's
implicit withdraw; those are counted separately, as
.B Duplicates
under the prefix statistics of
.BR "show ip bgp neighbors" .

The hold time reported by
.B show ip bgp neighbors
is the configured one, not the negotiated one, which the BGP library keeps
private.

.SH PAGING
Output is not paged. Piping a whole-table dump into a pager is inadvisable:
the daemon aborts a dump whose reader stops draining, so a pager that stops
at the first screen will truncate it. When that happens
.B netom\-cli
reports the truncation and exits non-zero rather than presenting a partial
table as a complete one.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command could not be parsed.
.TP
.B 2
The daemon could not be reached, or the response was truncated.
.TP
.B 3
The daemon returned an error.

.SH SECURITY
netom's HTTP API is unauthenticated and unencrypted. Pointing
.B \-\-url
at a non-loopback host sends queries, and receives configuration and
routing data, in the clear.
.B show running\-config
redacts secrets (BGP TCP-MD5 keys and MQTT passwords) but still exposes
topology: peer addresses, ASNs and listen ports.

.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/netom/netom.conf
Consulted for the endpoint when no
.B \-\-url
or
.B \-c
is given.
.TP
.B $XDG_STATE_HOME/netom/cli_history
Interactive command history. Falls back to
.B $HOME/.local/state/netom/cli_history
and, where neither is writable, to memory only.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR netom (1)
